"'''Need You Now'''" is a song recorded by American [[country music]] trio [[Lady Antebellum]] (now known as Lady A). The band co-wrote the song with [[Josh Kear]], and produced it with [[Paul Worley]]. It served as the lead single and title track to their second studio album [[Need You Now (Lady Antebellum album)|of the same name]], and was first released in the US on August 11, 2009, and it features lead vocals from both Scott and Kelley.<ref name=usrelease>{{cite web|url=http://musicremedy.com/l/lady-antebellum/videos/need-you-now-37510.html|title="Need You Now" US release date|access-date=September 26, 2010|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090921000124/http://musicremedy.com/l/lady-antebellum/videos/need-you-now-37510.html|archive-date=September 21, 2009}}</ref><ref name=iTunes-US>{{cite web|title=Need You Now – Single by Lady Antebellum|url=https://itunes.apple.com/us/album/need-you-now-single/id325126782|website=[[iTunes Store]] (US)|publisher=[[Apple Inc.]]|access-date=April 10, 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091119103228/http://itunes.apple.com/us/album/need-you-now-single/id325126782|archive-date=November 19, 2009}}</ref> The song also served as their debut single in the [[UK]] and [[Europe]], where it was released May 3, 2010. It won four [[Grammy Awards]] in 2011, including for [[Grammy Award for Song of the Year|Song of the Year]] and [[Record of the Year]].

The song spent five weeks at No. 1 on the ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' [[Hot Country Songs]] chart in late 2009.<ref name="countrystart">{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/charts/2009-11-28/country-songs|title=Country top 10 for chart week of November 28, 2009|magazine=Billboard.com|access-date=September 26, 2010}}</ref><ref name="countryend">{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/charts/2009-12-26/country-songs|title=Country top 10 for chart week of December 26, 2009|magazine=Billboard.com|access-date=September 26, 2010}}</ref> Thereafter, "Need You Now" crossed over onto various pop and adult contemporary music charts, becoming a top five hit in Canada, Ireland, and New Zealand, as well as a top ten hit in the Netherlands and Norway. The song won Single of the Year and Song of the Year at the 2010 [[Academy of Country Music]] Awards,<ref name="Country Music Television">{{cite web|url=http://www.cmt.com/news/country-music/1637295/miranda-lambert-lady-antebellum-carrie-underwood-reign-at-acm-awards.jhtml |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100419101615/http://www.cmt.com/news/country-music/1637295/miranda-lambert-lady-antebellum-carrie-underwood-reign-at-acm-awards.jhtml |url-status=dead |archive-date=April 19, 2010 |title=Miranda Lambert, Lady Antebellum, Carrie Underwood Reign at ACM Awards |publisher=CMT.com |access-date=April 20, 2010}}</ref> as well as Group Video of the Year at the 2010 [[CMT Music Awards#2010|CMT Music Awards]].<ref name="CMT Awards">{{cite web|url=http://www.cmt.com/cmt-music-awards/nominees.jhtml|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080208113542/http://www.cmt.com/cmt-music-awards/nominees.jhtml|url-status=dead|archive-date=February 8, 2008|title=2010 CMT Music Awards : Nominees|publisher=[[Country Music Television]]|access-date=April 24, 2010}}</ref> For the chart week of March 30, 2010, the song became the group's highest-charting single on the ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' [[Billboard Hot 100|Hot 100]], reaching No. 2,<ref name="billboardpeak">{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/#/charts/hot-100?chartDate=2010-03-30|title=Hot 100 top 10 for chart week of March 30, 2010|magazine=Billboard.com|access-date=September 26, 2010}}</ref> the best position for a country song by a band on that chart since [[Lonestar]]'s "[[Amazed]]" topped the tally at the beginning of the decade.<ref name="billboardpeak2">{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/charts/hot-100/2000-03-04|title=Hot 100 top 10 for chart week of March 4, 2000|magazine=Billboard.com|access-date=September 26, 2010}}</ref> It spent 60 weeks on the chart.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lady A {{!}} Biography, Music & News |url=https://www.billboard.com/artist/lady-antebellum/ |website=billboard.com}}</ref> The single has been [[RIAA certifications|certified 12× platinum]] by the [[Recording Industry Association of America]] (RIAA).<ref name="riaa.org">{{cite web|url= https://www.riaa.com/gold-platinum/?tab_active=default-award&ar=Lady+A&ti=Need+You+Now&format=Single&type=#search_section |title=RIAA - Gold & Platinum: Lady A, Need You Now|publisher=[[Recording Industry Association of America]] |access-date=August 26, 2025}}</ref>

A music video was shot for the song, directed by Dave McClister. In the video the song has an extended piano intro, and features all members of the group acting out scenes related to the storyline.<ref name="musicvideo">{{cite web|url=http://www.cmt.com/videos/lady-antebellum/438918/need-you-now.jhtml#fbid=CycKXIyx2gS|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090927015359/http://www.cmt.com/videos/lady-antebellum/438918/need-you-now.jhtml?#fbid=CycKXIyx2gS|url-status=dead|archive-date=September 27, 2009|title=Music video of "Need You Now"|publisher=CMT.com|access-date=September 26, 2010}}</ref> The song was initially released only to the country radio format in the United States and Canada on August 24, 2009,<ref name=usrelease/> but was remixed and re-released to all other formats domestically and internationally at the beginning of 2010. The song gained prominence internationally, in Europe and South America. The trio re-recorded the song again in [[Simlish]] to accompany the release of the ''[[The Sims 3|Sims 3]]'' expansion pack ''[[The Sims 3: Ambitions|Ambitions]]''.<ref name="simsversion">{{cite web|url=http://www.marketwatch.com/story/rise-against-lady-antebellum-melanie-fiona-and-toni-braxton-sing-hit-songs-for-eas-the-sims-3-ambitions-expansion-pack-2010-05-18?reflink=MW_news_stmp |title=Lady Antebellum records "Need You Now" in Simlish |access-date=September 26, 2010 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100523050002/http://www.marketwatch.com/story/rise-against-lady-antebellum-melanie-fiona-and-toni-braxton-sing-hit-songs-for-eas-the-sims-3-ambitions-expansion-pack-2010-05-18?reflink=MW_news_stmp |archive-date=May 23, 2010 }}</ref> By April 17, 2011, the song became the ninth most downloaded song in history, moving five million copies, and surpassed Taylor Swift's "[[Love Story (Taylor Swift song)|Love Story]]" as the most downloaded country song in history.<ref>{{cite web| url=http://new.music.yahoo.com/blogs/chart_watch/74350/chart-watch-extra-lady-a-makes-country-history/| title=Chart Watch Extra: Lady A Makes Country History| last=Grein| first=Paul| date=April 7, 2011| access-date=March 15, 2013| work=[[Yahoo! Music]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://new.music.yahoo.com/blogs/chart_watch/74355/week-ending-april-17-2011-songs-youth-will-be-served/ |title=Week Ending April 17, 2011. Songs: Youth Will Be Served |work=Yahoo! Music |last=Grein |first=Paul |access-date=March 15, 2013 |date=April 20, 2011 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110424213038/http://new.music.yahoo.com/blogs/chart_watch/74355/week-ending-april-17-2011-songs-youth-will-be-served/ |archive-date=April 24, 2011 }}</ref> It has since sold over 6 million copies in the US.<ref name="yahoo_jan2013">{{cite news |url=http://music.yahoo.com/blogs/chart-watch/week-ending-dec-30-2012-songs-taylor-knew-173439422.html|title=Week Ending Dec. 30, 2012. Songs: Taylor Knew Bruno Was Trouble|author=Paul Grein|work=Chart Watch|publisher=Yahoo Music |date=January 4, 2013 |access-date=January 5, 2013 }}</ref>

